ps://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-03-05T00:21:43Z","updated_at":"2023-03-05T00:21:43Z","body":"@bojanHub\r\n\r\nA crash issue occurred related to Pull Request #2048.\r\n\r\nAny idea to solve this issue?\r\n\r\nThanks a lot!\r\nSukchan","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1454934546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1455646676","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115#issuecomment-1455646676","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115","id":1455646676,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5Ww2fU","user":{"login":"bojanHub","id":83633896,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMzODk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83633896?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub","html_url":"https://github.com/bojanHub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-03-06T07:58:47Z","updated_at":"2023-03-06T07:58:47Z","body":"I have no deep knowledge of everything about open5gs but according to logs it looks to me like new PFCP session wanted to be established:\r\n`02/28 14:32:27.283: [smf] DEBUG: Session Establishment Request (../src/smf/n4-build.c:45)\r\n`\r\n\r\nAnd I guess this new session was already put in the session list: `smf_ue->sess_list`\r\n\r\nSoon after that there were no response on 3 PFCP heartbeats and so we get:\r\n```\r\n02/28 14:32:28.033: [smf] DEBUG: smf_state_operational(): SMF_EVT_N4_NO_HEARTBEAT (../src/smf/smf-sm.c:83)\r\n02/28 14:32:28.033: [smf] DEBUG: smf_pfcp_state_associated(): SMF_EVT_N4_NO_HEARTBEAT (../src/smf/pfcp-sm.c:166)\r\n```\r\nI am not sure if this is true but my assumption is that above session does not have sm_context_ref but anyway was in the list `smf_ue->sess_list` and so we got this:\r\n02/28 14:32:28.033: [smf] FATAL: smf_npcf_smpolicycontrol_build_delete: Assertion `sess->sm_context_ref' failed.\r\n\r\nOne solution maybe to put additional \"condition\" here:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncase SMF_EVT_N4_NO_HEARTBEAT:\r\n...\r\n            ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_ue->sess_list, next, sess) {\r\n                ogs_assert(sess);\r\n\r\n                if ((node == sess->pfcp_node) && (sess->sm_context_ref))  {   <---- (sess->sm_context_ref)\r\n                    smf_npcf_smpolicycontrol_param_t param;\r\n\r\n                    memset(&param, 0, sizeof(param));\r\n                    ogs_assert(true ==\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut I am not sure if then will be everything ok about freeing the resources for this started session?\r\nOr if there is any possibility to not allow SMF to choose such UPF (sess->pfcp_node) if there is at least one heartbeat without response? In this case this problematic session will not be connected to this `sess->pfcp_node` and so if condition will be false and `smf_npcf_smpolicycontrol_build_delete` will not be called. \r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1455646676/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1456013961","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115#issuecomment-1456013961","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115","id":1456013961,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5WyQKJ","user":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-03-06T12:06:03Z","updated_at":"2023-03-06T12:06:03Z","body":"@Sabreu and @bojanHub \r\n\r\nI think I've found the cause of the problem. There were two problems. \r\n\r\nFirst of all, the 'next' variable is used simultaneously in two for-loops. We need to fix this as below.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n$ diff --git a/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c b/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c\r\nindex 348ef3472..9a1f95f8e 100644\r\n--- a/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c\r\n+++ b/src/smf/pfcp-sm.c\r\n@@ -319,13 +319,13 @@ void smf_pfcp_state_associated(ogs_fsm_t *s, smf_event_t *e)\r\n         node = e->pfcp_node;\r\n         ogs_assert(node);\r\n \r\n-        smf_ue_t *smf_ue = NULL, *next = NULL;;\r\n+        smf_ue_t *smf_ue = NULL, *next_ue = NULL;;\r\n \r\n-        ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_self()->smf_ue_list, next, smf_ue) {\r\n-            smf_sess_t *sess = NULL, *next = NULL;;\r\n+        ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_self()->smf_ue_list, next_ue, smf_ue) {\r\n+            smf_sess_t *sess = NULL, *next_sess = NULL;;\r\n             ogs_assert(smf_ue);\r\n \r\n-            ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_ue->sess_list, next, sess) {\r\n+            ogs_list_for_each_safe(&smf_ue->sess_list, next_sess, sess) {\r\n                 ogs_assert(sess);\r\n \r\n                 if (node == sess->pfcp_node) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nSecond, the 'node' variable was already deleted in ogs_pfcp_xact_delete() after N4 timeout. Therefore, we should not use 'node' variables passed using message queue.\r\n\r\nSo, I've fixed it.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if you have any other idea.\r\n\r\nThank you so much for raising this issue.\r\nSukchan\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1456013961/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1456032802","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115#issuecomment-1456032802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115","id":1456032802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5WyUwi","user":{"login":"bojanHub","id":83633896,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNjMzODk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83633896?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub","html_url":"https://github.com/bojanHub","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bojanHub/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-03-06T12:18:33Z","updated_at":"2023-03-06T12:18:33Z","body":"@acetcom\r\n\r\nGreat and sorry for problems :)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1456032802/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1457626793","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115#issuecomment-1457626793","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2115","id":1457626793,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5W4Z6p","user":{"login":"Sabreu","id":1567864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1Njc4NjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1567864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sabreu","html_url":"https://github.com/Sabreu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sabreu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sabr